// Contract refinement across files, where the inherited slot's parameter is a GENERIC INSTANCE.
// A refining contract merges its parent's methods, and those signatures were written — and resolve —
// in the PARENT's file. Re-resolving them in the child's namespace named a bare, undeclared `View` in
// the emitted vtable unless the child's file happened to import `View` too, which it has no reason to.
// See linkContracts: an inherited signature is rebound to its parent-resolved absolute spelling at
// merge time, so the slot mangles identically no matter which file emits it.
namespace crgen::crbase;
import std::collections::{View};
export { Parent };
type contract Parent for resource {
    fn int32 take(View<uint8> bytes);
}
